With the frontend's block config (`CONTENT_SCHEMAS`), the mock API gives content read from markdown the search text the editor's save would write, for every block that stores none, so pages are found by their words locally and once deployed. Markdown may store a block's `searchableText` (as a field, or made by a prototype from the page's words); a markdown export leaves out what matches the default. Decoding still needs nothing but the page. Markdown no longer carries a Text block's `plaintext`: drop `plaintext="${…/text}"` from your Text-block prototypes; a prototype that makes it is refused.
